      "expect": {
        "ok": true
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "validate/nullable/null-rejected-on-non-nullable-scalar",
      "spec": "docs/03-schema-model.md#35-nullable-versus-optional",
      "operation": "validate",
      "purpose": "error-case",
      "input": {
        "schema": "record R {\n    \"n\": string,\n}\nroot R\n",
        "document": {
          "edges": [
            [
              "n",
              {
                "scalar": {
                  "kind": null,
                  "value": null
                }
              }
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "ok": false,
        "diagnostics": [
          {
            "path": "$.n",
            "code": "validate.null-not-allowed"
          }
        ]
      },
      "comment": "No `?` on the field, so null is never checked against kind and is rejected outright -- distinct from a nullable field (already covered by validate/basic/nullable-scalar-accepts-null)."
    },
    {
      "name": "validate/any/any-accepts-null",
      "spec": "docs/03-schema-model.md#37-the-any-type",
      "operation": "validate",
      "purpose": "edge-case",
      "input": {
        "schema": "record R {\n    \"data\": any,\n}\nroot R\n",
        "document": {
          "edges": [
            [
              "data",
              {
                "scalar": {
                  "kind": null,
                  "value": null
                }
              }
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "ok": true
      },
      "comment": "any admits null with no nullable-scalar mechanism needed -- any already includes null by definition (Sec3.7), which is also why any? is rejected as redundant."
    },
    {
      "name": "validate/any/any-accepts-a-bare-scalar-not-just-a-subtree",
      "spec": "docs/03-schema-model.md#37-the-any-type",
      "operation": "validate",
      "purpose": "edge-case",
      "input": {
        "schema": "record R {\n    \"data\": any,\n}\nroot R\n",
        "document": {
          "edges": [
            [
              "data",
              {
                "scalar": {
                  "kind": "integer",
                  "value": 42
                }
              }
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "ok": true
      },
      "comment": "The existing any/descent-stops-at-any vector uses a nested node payload; this companion vector confirms any also accepts a bare scalar directly, since any accepts every legal Document value: any scalar of any kind, null, and any node."
    }
